<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!-- The buttons for home and work, lying down (SPEC §7.1): a second
         column just to the start of the right-hand one, home level with
         "locate me" and work level with the journey button.

         Standing up they head the right-hand column, but a phone on its side
         has some 410dp of height, and seven buttons of 48dp with their gaps do
         not fit in it: the column climbed into the top row and the work button
         came to lie over the settings, which could no longer be pressed. Beside
         the column, nothing they add climbs towards the top row, and a button
         that comes or goes still moves none of the others.

         They start at "locate me" rather than at the journey button so as to
         leave the compass its row. With home level with the journey button,
         work rose into the height of the top row, in the very column the
         compass appears in once the map is turned, and on a Fairphone 3 the
         two overlapped by 14 px.

         The shift is one button and one gap (touch_target_min plus space_s);
         values/dimens.xml says how the two figures are read. -->
    <dimen name="saved_place_button_shift">56dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="saved_place_button_lift">0dp</dimen>

</resources>
